     The function rreeaallhhoossttnnaammee__ssaa() converts _a_d_d_r to the corresponding host
     name.  This is done by resolving _a_d_d_r to a host name and then ensuring
     that the host name resolves back to _a_d_d_r.

     _h_o_s_t must point to a buffer of at least _h_s_i_z_e bytes, and will always be
     written to by this function.

     If the name resolution does not work both ways or if the host name is
     longer than _h_s_i_z_e bytes, getnameinfo(3) with NI_NUMERICHOST specified, is
     used to convert _a_d_d_r to an ASCII form.

     If the string written to _h_o_s_t is _h_s_i_z_e bytes long, _h_o_s_t will not be NUL
     terminated.

